				"name": "CatalogWriteService.constructor.adapter",
				"type": "SqliteAdapter",
				"required": true,
				"description": "The SqliteAdapter that replace() writes through: replace() runs all of its work in one adapter.transaction() call, clears each catalog model table with adapter.execute() and inserts each row with adapter.insert(). The constructor only stores it as a private readonly field and makes no database call."
			},
			{
				"name": "CatalogWriteService.replace.index",
				"type": "HistoryIndex",
				"required": true,
				"description": "The history index that every replace() call projects: each branch becomes a catalog branch row keyed by its name and holding its head, and each revision becomes a row keyed by its commit, with each record keyed by JSON.stringify([commit, record id]). The whole index is also hashed with stableJson and its SHA-256 digest is stored in the catalog metadata row; the index is used as given and is not validated here.",
